SRP630949	SRX30813164	Oseltamivir and baloxavir monotherapy and combination therapy efficacy against clade 2.3.4.4b A(H5N1) influenza virus infection in ferrets	11320	Influenza A virus	AMPLICON	VIRAL RNA	PCR	SRS26825019	T7544-mock-NT-2-4	Illumina iSeq 100	79346	7566572	SRR35763863	79346	21133174	T7544-mock-NT-2-4	viral RNA extraction with Qiagen followed by PCR with influenza virus universal primers. Sequenced with Illumina iSeq	T7544-mock-NT-2-4	ILLUMINA	SRS26825019	PAIRED	SAMN52624397	SRS26825019	21133174		Influenza A virus	T7544-mock-NT-2-4	11320	T7544-mock-NT-2-4_S2_L001_R1_001.fastq.gz	5579846	5019542	5064047	51730	5418009	fastq	s3.us-east-1	s3	run	s3.us-east-1	s3	run.zq	gs.us-east1	gs	run.zq	s3.us-east-1	s3	public	"<Database><Table name=""SEQUENCE""><Statistics source=""meta""><Rows count=""79346"" /><Elements count=""21133174"" /></Statistics></Table></Database>"	1	true	true	2025-10-31 03:15:20	Use Cloud Data Delivery	-	AWS	s3://sra-pub-src-16/SRR35763863/T7544-mock-NT-2-4_S2_L001_R1_001.fastq.gz.1	public	2025-10-09 13:22:44	T7544-mock-NT-2-4_S2_L001_R1_001.fastq.gz	007e8d304375aa1ec161e33ec63d8ca2	fastq	6073712	0	Original	1	Use Cloud Data Delivery	-	AWS	s3://sra-pub-src-16/SRR35763863/T7544-mock-NT-2-4_S2_L001_R2_001.fastq.gz.1	public	2025-10-09 13:22:41	T7544-mock-NT-2-4_S2_L001_R2_001.fastq.gz	a7cc2969e5f96d520e39d473a9df95f1	fastq	6298874	0	Original	1	anonymous	worldwide	AWS	https://sra-pub-run-odp.s3.amazonaws.com/sra/SRR35763863/SRR35763863	public	2025-10-09 13:22:55	SRR35763863	188c28ce4889ae75571c0f9c2fd707cb	SRA Normalized	7569383	1	Primary ETL	https://sra-pub-run-odp.s3.amazonaws.com/sra/SRR35763863/SRR35763863	1	anonymous	worldwide	NCBI	https://sra-downloadb.be-md.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sos9/sra-pub-zq-924/SRR035/35763/SRR35763863/SRR35763863.lite.1	aws identity	s3.us-east-1	AWS	s3://sra-pub-zq-9/SRR35763863/SRR35763863.lite.1	gcp identity	gs.us-east1	GCP	gs://sra-pub-zq-103/SRR35763863/SRR35763863.lite.1	public	2025-10-09 15:57:25	SRR35763863.lite	051d56d937069666313a86f0b6b15268	SRA Lite	5691247	1	Primary ETL	https://sra-downloadb.be-md.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sos9/sra-pub-zq-924/SRR035/35763/SRR35763863/SRR35763863.lite.1	1	1	21133174	false	21133174	7566572	1	79346	BioSampleModel	Pathogen.cl	strain	A/Washington/239/2024	isolate	T7544-mock-NT-2-4	collected_by	CDC ID PLT	collection_date	2025-05	geo_loc_name	USA: Georgia	host	Mustela putorius furo	host_disease	Influenza A	isolation_source	ferret	lat_lon	33.79807962 N 84.32742576 W	SAMN52624397	BioSample	XREF_LINK	DB: bioproject	ID: 1339024	LABEL: PRJNA1339024	PRJNA1339024	BioProject	PRJNA1339024	BioProject	XREF_LINK	DB: pubmed	ID: 41588212	Neuraminidase inhibitors (NAIs) and cap-dependent endonuclease inhibitors (CENIs) represent two classes of antiviral drugs recommended for early treatment of patients with seasonal influenza A virus (IAV) infections. However, only limited human data, particularly on combination antiviral treatment, are available to inform optimal dosing regimens against novel IAVs, including highly pathogenic avian influenza A(H5N1) virus, associated with severe disease. Clade 2.3.4.4b A(H5N1) viruses have caused outbreaks in avian and mammalian species worldwide, highlighting the need to assess antiviral drug efficacy against these strains. We challenged ferrets with a D1.1 genotype A(H5N1) virus and treated infected animals with the NAI oseltamivir phosphate (OST) and the CENI baloxavir acid (BXA), alone or in combination, with treatment onset commencing pre- or post-symptom onset (24- or 48-hours post-inoculation (p.i.), respectively). When administered pre- or post-illness onset, BXA, but not OST, monotherapy provided significant reduction of clinical signs and significantly decreased infectious viral levels (in both respiratory and extrapulmonary specimens) compared with mock-treated animals. Combination OST/BXA treatment, when administered pre- or post-symptom onset, resulted in significant improvements in both metrics versus OST monotherapy. These data support continued investigation of antiviral treatment modalities that include both NAI and CENI for patients with mild and severe A(H5N1) disease.	Oseltamivir and baloxavir monotherapy and combination therapy efficacy against clade 2.3.4.4b A(H5N1) influenza virus infection in ferrets	Other	SRA2245655	SUB15691868	Centers for Disease Control and Prevention	Influenza Division
